/*
 * Generic MT7615 calibration/EEPROM blob for cards with no factory
 * calibration in eFuse or flash (chip-id 0x7615 verified at offset 0).
 *
 * Source: https://tmshlvck.github.io/blog/2025/12/04/2025-12-mt7615e-eeprom-bpir4/
 * ("mt7615e_rf.bin", 19880 bytes), published by that post's author for
 * exactly this problem (MT7615E cards with no onboard eeprom chip).
 * Used here via the mainline mt76 driver's native `mediatek,eeprom-data`
 * devicetree property (mt76_get_of_eeprom_data() in eeprom.c) -- no kernel
 * patch needed, unlike the filesystem-loading approach described there.
 *
 * This is a generic calibration, not any specific unit's own factory
 * calibration -- regulatory accuracy (exact per-channel/country max TX
 * power) and RF performance are "good enough", not per-unit optimized.
 * See BOOTLOADER-PATCH.md / README.md for context on when this is needed.
